---
title: Chemex Hot
coffee:
  id: chemex-hot
  brewer: chemex
  brewerName: Chemex
  label: Hot
  legacyVariant: hot
  size: "6–8 cup"
  min: 20
  max: 45
  dose: 30
  grind: Encore · 20
  texture: Start medium-coarse, like coarse sand. Original Encore, not ESP. Adjust to taste; calibration varies.
  temperature: 201–205°F
  temperatureF: 203
  order: 30
  icon: "⋈"
  description: Smooth & easygoing
---

= Prep =
Place the three-layer side of the filter against the spout. Rinse, then discard the rinse water. Add @coffee{30%g} to the #Chemex{} and make a small well in the center.

= Bloom =
Wet all the grounds with @water{90%g} over ~{15%seconds}, then give the brewer a gentle swirl.

= Let it bloom =
Let the coffee release its gas. No water needed. Wait until ~until{45%seconds} on the brew clock.

= Pour 1 =
Pour @water{130%g} over ~{35%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Let it settle =
Give the water time to drain through the bed for ~{20%seconds}.

= Pour 2 =
Pour @water{130%g} over ~{35%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Let it settle =
Give the water time to drain through the bed for ~{20%seconds}.

= Pour 3 =
Pour @water{130%g} over ~{35%seconds} in slow circles, from the center outward. Avoid the filter walls.

= Draw down =
Gently swirl to level the bed. Let the remaining water drain until ~until{270%seconds} on the brew clock.

= Finish =
Swirl, sip, and tell your journal how it went.
